\pard\f2\b\fs28\fi-1020\li1200\fc0\cf0 Class Description\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\f0\b0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 The NSCharacterSet class declares the programmatic interface for an object that manages a set of Unicode characters (see the NSString class cluster specification for information on Unicode). NSCharacterSet's principal primitive method, 
\b characterIsMember:
\b0 , provides the basis for all other instance methods in its interface. A subclass of NSCharacterSet needs only to implement this method, plus 
\b mutableCopyWithZone:
\b0 , for proper behavior. For optimal performance, a subclass should also override 
\b bitmapRepresentation
\b0  which otherwise works by invoking 
\b characterIsMember:
\b0  for every possible Unicode value.\

\fs14 \

