\pard\f2\b\fs28\fi-1020\li1200\fc0\cf0 Class Description\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\f0\b0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 The NSMutableCharacterSet class declares the programmatic interface to objects that manage a modifiable set of Unicode characters. You can add or remove characters from a mutable character set as numeric values in NSRanges or as character values in strings; combine character sets by union or intersection; and invert a character set.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 Mutable character sets are less efficient to use than immutable character sets. If you don't need to change a character set after creating it, create an immutable copy with 
\b copy
\b0  and use that.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSMutableCharacterSet defines no primitive methods. Subclasses must implement all methods declared by this class in addition to the primitives of NSCharacterSet. They must also implement 
\b mutableCopyWithZone:
\b0 .\

